  "authoringNote": "The order states its treating practitioner by name only (identifier null). SPEC R03 accepts a practitioner name or identifier, so R03 passes on the permitted name alternative with eight citations; the null identifier is not a fact, is not cited and is never required or invented. R04 compares practitioner sameness by identifier only (C03; oracle decision 5): the pair of the final encounter (SYN-PRAC-0001) and the final order (no identifier) holds R04.practitioner_identifier_absent, manual_review for the administrative reviewer, even though both name the same practitioner, because a name-only comparison is not treated as verified identity. R04 cites the encounter status, date and practitioner identifier and the order status and date (five). The dates are in sequence and within the C01 bound 2027-02-20, so no chronology condition holds; no parent document is named (C07). The receipt follows the order date span (C06), so R05 passes. R01, R02, R07, R08 and R09 pass, R06 is qualified clinical review with five clinical citations and no administrative effect, and R10 is not applicable. The state is needs_human_review through R04 only.",
